 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Generally it goes by each person contributing a set amount rather than a share of the total cost. That way there's no surprises who ends up as the host. Then ask them to contribute according to the typical system. Weddings are supposed to be fun, not a test of who has the most money. Not at all. Weddings are shared gifts, not individual ones. Then you could ask if there's a deadline for deciding, and if they still won't contribute, you could go ahead without them. Weddings needn't be about anyone who can't make it. Good idea. Weddings are shared gifts, after all.",
